Ungate the SVG pointer-events keywords in stylo's Servo build.

This targets the STYLO repository (https://github.com/servo/stylo), not
servo — it sits outside the numbered servo series, like stylo-0001.

SVG 2 defines pointer-events: visiblePainted | visibleFill | visibleStroke
| visible | painted | fill | stroke | all | none, and stylo has every one
of them — behind #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]. Servo is therefore left with
auto and none, so nothing in an SVG can say "hit my stroke but not my
fill", which is most of what the property is for. The values are plain
keywords with no Gecko-specific machinery behind them; the gate looks
like an artefact of Gecko having been the only consumer.

Note the single-capital spelling of the variants, which is load-bearing:
the Parse derive lowercases CamelCase into kebab-case, so VisiblePainted
would parse as `visible-painted`. Visiblepainted gives `visiblepainted`,
which matches the spec's `visiblePainted` because CSS keywords are ASCII
case-insensitive. Left as-is, and commented so it survives a tidy-up.

Consumed by servo patch 0011 (SVG hit testing), which maps the full set
onto fill and stroke hit regions. Servo's existing uses of the property
only ever compare against None, so ungating cannot change their meaning.

To try it: check out stylo at the rev pinned in servo's Cargo.lock,
apply, and add a [patch."https://github.com/servo/stylo"] section
redirecting all eleven stylo-repo crates at the local checkout.

diff --git a/style/values/specified/ui.rs b/style/values/specified/ui.rs
index d5d368b18..6b01b3cc2 100644
--- a/style/values/specified/ui.rs
+++ b/style/values/specified/ui.rs
@@ -284,21 +284,18 @@ pub enum MozTheme {
 pub enum PointerEvents {
     Auto,
     None,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
+    // Note the single-capital spelling: the `Parse` derive lowercases a
+    // CamelCase variant into kebab-case, so `VisiblePainted` would parse as
+    // `visible-painted`. `Visiblepainted` gives `visiblepainted`, which
+    // matches the spec's `visiblePainted` because CSS keywords are ASCII
+    // case-insensitive.
     Visiblepainted,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
     Visiblefill,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
     Visiblestroke,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
     Visible,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
     Painted,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
     Fill,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
     Stroke,
-    #[cfg(feature = "gecko")]
     All,
 }
 
